full-query: "A team has implemented a service with AWS API Gateway and Lambda. The service endpoint can save input JSON data to the internal database and S3 After the service has run for several years, some data in the JSON body are no longer used and should not be saved anymore. The backend Lambda has been upgraded to support only the valid JSON values. The original API in API Gateway is still used for some time before all users migrate to the new API. How should the original API be configured so that the Lambda still supports the old request in the backend?"
